From 43369309302e5645b41826373ad0bb69ba4ccbb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joaocarvalhosm <119947699+joaocarvalhosm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:06:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: hp-wmi: Add Victus 15-fb2xxx (8C2F) support

The HP Victus 15-fb2xxx (Ryzen 8000 series, board name 8C2F) uses
the same Victus S WMI interface as the other boards already listed
with victus_s_board_params, but is missing from the board table.

Without the entry the driver exposes only a two-state pwm1_enable,
registers no platform profile, and leaves the embedded controller on
its most conservative fan curve: under sustained load the CPU reaches
its 100 C limit while both fans remain stopped. The NVIDIA driver also
fails to read its target temperature and platform power mode from the
SBIOS, because the thermal profile is never initialised.

Add the board so it gets the Victus S thermal profiles, GPU cTGP/PPAB
switching, fan RPM readout and manual fan control.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
index 615b4cf..7e13652 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
@@ -299,6 +299,10 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id hp_wmi_feature_boards[] __initconst = {
 		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8BD5") },
 		.driver_data = (void *)&victus_s_board_params,
 	},
+	{
+		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8C2F") },
+		.driver_data = (void *)&victus_s_board_params,
+	},
 	{
 		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8C76") },
 		.driver_data = (void *)&omen_v1_board_params,
-- 
2.53.0

